# Ocentra Parent Validation Rules

Run the smallest useful check that proves the assigned slice. Do not escalate validation by habit.

When working through `docs/repo-audits/lane-manager-coordination/`, first read:

- `docs/repo-audits/lane-manager-coordination/VALIDATION_BUDGET_LADDER.md`

## Slice validation rule

| Work type | Default validation |
| --- | --- |
| docs-only / inventory-only | path checks and `git diff --check` on touched docs only |
| touched script | syntax/static check for the touched script plus exact proof command only if assigned |
| touched package source | targeted package test for touched file or owner package |
| touched Rust crate source | targeted `cargo test -p <crate> <filter>` or assigned crate check |
| touched UI proof | one assigned test/spec, not full UI suite |
| final PR/main-lane readiness | explicit full gate if assigned by coordinator |

## Main Gate

```powershell
npm run validate
```

This is a final readiness gate, not a default slice handoff gate.

Do not run it for normal plan slices, docs-only work, audit inventory, or proof-root normalization unless the dispatch packet explicitly says to run it.

## Supporting Gates

Use supporting gates only when scoped to touched files, packages, or crates.

```powershell
npm run build
npm run format:check
npm run security:scan-repo
cargo test
```

The unscoped forms above are not default slice commands. Prefer workspace/package/crate/touched-file forms named by the assigned workpack.

Architecture policy gates:

```powershell
npm run lint:architecture -- --files <touched-file-or-dir> [more files or dirs]
cargo lint-architecture <touched-rs-file-or-dir> [more files or dirs]
```

Use directory paths to run the same hard gate per module, crate, or domain without waiting for full validation.

For PR diffs or full debt sweeps, use the explicit diff or all-files forms only when assigned:

```powershell
npm run lint:architecture -- --base <base> --head <head>
npm run lint:architecture:all
cargo lint-architecture --base <base> --head <head>
cargo lint-architecture --all
```

`lint:architecture` covers:

- TypeScript/JavaScript and Rust re-export bans
- no validation-bypass directives
- no focused/skipped/todo tests
- no weak test assertions
- no placeholder implementation markers in production source
- import ownership boundaries
- Rust raw domain primitive bans
- Rust string-boundary checks
- Rust dependency policy checks

## Stale Dev Services

If `cargo build` or `cargo test` cannot overwrite the service binary on Windows, check whether the dev service is still running on port `4477` and stop it before rebuilding.

Parent fixed ports are `4477` for the headless Rust agent and `4478` for the
dev portal. LAN mode uses the same ports through `npm run dev:lan`. Do not use
generic Vite port `5173` or the Ocentra Games asset-editor port `5174`.

If smoke tests need ports, make sure stale processes are not providing a fake pass. Use the managed scripts in `scripts/dev/` so only clearly Ocentra Parent processes are reclaimed.

## Validation Reports

Report exact commands run, exact validation level, exact failures, and which broader gates were intentionally skipped. Do not summarize a failed gate as "mostly passing".
